From 6c32721012e37b1aa145d36fad16c1ce021cd3f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:35:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/71] fix(executorch): keep a failed classifier load from
 evicting resident models

A failed et-server load used to fall into the Router's nuclear path: evict
every loaded model, then load the classifier a second time. An OOM-killed load
on a small gateway therefore cost the resident LLM and repeated the load that
had just been killed.

- error_types: NonRetryableLoadException; Router::load_error_skips_nuclear_retry
  treats it, and the existing file-not-found messages, as rethrow-only.
- executorch: every load failure is non-retryable. Only SIGKILL skips the
  stderr-capture relaunch; cancel and the readiness timeout (child still
  running) now throw at once instead of relaunching; other signals and exits
  keep the capture and report the signal or code with it.
- executorch: choose_port() instead of an unchecked find_free_port; classify
  text over 1 MiB is refused with 413; include order and continuation alignment.
- test_backend_load_failure (cpp-ci): classification of load errors and
  startup_exit_code() for SIGKILL, exit 3, cancel and timeout children.

